   "text": "The rule the Department inherited: control, popular assent and obligations (1877-1900)",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "These five papers show the rule the Department started with. Each states a test of fact (control, the people's assent, the ability to meet obligations) rather than of legality, and the Mexican papers of 1877 and 1878 show the test used as a price: recognition was held back until frontier raids eased and claims were paid."
